---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Leaderboard from '../components/Leaderboard.astro';
import WaitlistForm from '../components/WaitlistForm.astro';
import SpatialVisualization from '../components/SpatialVisualization.astro';

const title = 'Sky3 Network: Decentralized Trust for Spatial AI';
const description = 'Sky3 is building an independent benchmark for spatial AI. Engineers, hobbyists and researchers contribute edge-case data from the physical world, the community verifies it, and AI models are scored in public so vendors stop grading their own homework.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <Header />
  
  <main id="top">
    <section id="hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="hero-content">
          <div class="hero-text">
            <div class="kicker">OPEN PROTOCOL · DRAFT v0.1</div>
            <h1>Decentralized Trust for Spatial AI</h1>
            <p class="subhead">Sky3 is building an independent benchmark for spatial AI. Engineers, hobbyists and researchers contribute edge-case data from the physical world—the hard cases models fail on—the community verifies it, and AI models are scored in public so vendors stop grading their own homework.</p>
            
            <div class="cta-group">
              <a href="#waitlist" class="btn btn-primary">
                Join the early contributor waitlist
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M5 12h14"></path>
                  <path d="M12 5l7 7l-7 7"></path>
                </svg>
              </a>
              <a href="/roadmap" class="btn btn-secondary">View the roadmap</a>
            </div>
            
            <div class="hero-links">
              <a href="#manifesto" class="text-link">
                <span>Read the manifesto</span>
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M7 7l10 10"></path>
                  <path d="M17 8v9h-9"></path>
                </svg>
              </a>
              <span class="separator">·</span>
              <a href="#leaderboard" class="text-link">
                <span>See the sample leaderboard</span>
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M7 7l10 10"></path>
                  <path d="M17 8v9h-9"></path>
                </svg>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
          
          <div class="hero-visual">
            <SpatialVisualization />
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="fact-strip">
          <div class="fact-item">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M4 17v2a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2 -2v-2"></path>
              <path d="M7 9l5 -5l5 5"></path>
              <path d="M12 4l0 12"></path>
            </svg>
            <span>Contributors upload LiDAR scans, CAD files, robot logs and complex geometry imagery</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fact-item">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M9 12l2 2l4 -4"></path>
              <path d="M12 3a12 12 0 0 0 8.5 3a12 12 0 0 1 -8.5 15a12 12 0 0 1 -8.5 -15a12 12 0 0 0 8.5 -3"></path>
            </svg>
            <span>Independent reviewers verify every case before it counts toward a benchmark</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fact-item">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M3 12m0 1a1 1 0 0 1 1 -1h4a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v6a1 1 0 0 1 -1 1h-4a1 1 0 0 1 -1 -1z"></path>
              <path d="M9 8m0 1a1 1 0 0 1 1 -1h4a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v10a1 1 0 0 1 -1 1h-4a1 1 0 0 1 -1 -1z"></path>
              <path d="M15 4m0 1a1 1 0 0 1 1 -1h4a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1 -1 1h-4a1 1 0 0 1 -1 -1z"></path>
            </svg>
            <span>Models are scored in public on these verified real-world edge cases</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    
    <section id="manifesto">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label">MANIFESTO · DRAFT v0.1</div>
        <h2>Why spatial AI needs a neutral referee</h2>
        
        <div class="manifesto-body">
          <p>Models that reason about the physical world are moving from research into robots, factories and buildings. Today, the claims about how well they work mostly come from the people who built them, measured on benchmarks they chose.</p>
          
          <p>Simulation does not capture everything. A model that scores well on synthetic scenes can still misread a cluttered shelf, a non-standard fastener or a structure that only holds together because of one hidden joint. These gaps show up when a system is deployed, and that is the most expensive place to find them.</p>
          
          <p>Sky3 proposes a simple alternative: test models on real-world cases that the model's builders did not pick, and publish the results.</p>
        </div>
        
        <ol class="principles-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Independent.</strong> Benchmarks are run by the network, not by the teams whose models are being scored.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Grounded in the real world.</strong> Test cases come from physical scans, drawings and recordings, with a focus on rare and difficult cases.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Verified.</strong> Every contributed case is checked by automated tests and by human reviewers before it is used for scoring.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Reproducible.</strong> Metrics, scoring code and evaluation splits are published so anyone can check a result.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Private by default.</strong> Submissions are stripped of metadata, faces and identifying information before they enter the archive.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Community-governed.</strong> The test suite and the rules for changing it are governed by contributors and reviewers through an open process, stewarded by a non-profit foundation.
          </li>
        </ol>
        
        <p class="footnote">This is a draft. The protocol, metrics and governance model will change based on feedback from the beta.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    
    <section id="leaderboard">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label">SPATIAL LEADERBOARD · FORMAT PREVIEW</div>
        <h2>What a public scorecard looks like</h2>
        <p class="intro-text">The leaderboard will rank spatial and physical-world models on verified real-world cases. <strong>The table below shows the format only—all model names and scores are fictional</strong> to illustrate how results will be presented.</p>
        
        <Leaderboard />
      </div>
    </section>
    
    <section id="what-to-contribute">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label">FOR CONTRIBUTORS</div>
        <h2>What you'd upload, and why it matters</h2>
        
        <p class="intro-text">The benchmark will be built from edge cases that break current models. If you work with spatial data, you likely have examples that models consistently fail on.</p>
        
        <div class="contribution-examples">
          <div class="example-card">
            <div class="example-icon">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M3 12m0 1a1 1 0 0 1 1 -1h4a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v6a1 1 0 0 1 -1 1h-4a1 1 0 0 1 -1 -1z"></path>
                <path d="M9 8m0 1a1 1 0 0 1 1 -1h4a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v10a1 1 0 0 1 -1 1h-4a1 1 0 0 1 -1 -1z"></path>
                <path d="M15 4m0 1a1 1 0 0 1 1 -1h4a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1 -1 1h-4a1 1 0 0 1 -1 -1z"></path>
                <path d="M4 20l14 0"></path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>LiDAR and point clouds</h3>
            <p>Scans with reflective surfaces, glass facades, or extreme weather artifacts. Cases where reconstruction algorithms misread structure or merge unconnected parts.</p>
            <div class="example-formats">.las, .laz, .ply, .pcd</div>
          </div>
          
          <div class="example-card">
            <div class="example-icon">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M3 19a9 9 0 0 1 9 0a9 9 0 0 1 9 0"></path>
                <path d="M3 6a9 9 0 0 1 9 0a9 9 0 0 1 9 0"></path>
                <path d="M3 6l0 13"></path>
                <path d="M12 6l0 13"></path>
                <path d="M21 6l0 13"></path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>CAD and 3D models</h3>
            <p>Assemblies with non-standard fasteners, interference fits, or parts that only work in one configuration. Structures that look plausible but can't hold load.</p>
            <div class="example-formats">.step, .stl, .obj, .fbx</div>
          </div>
          
          <div class="example-card">
            <div class="example-icon">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M9 19c-4.3 1.4 -4.3 -2.5 -6 -3m12 5v-3.5c0 -1 .1 -1.4 -.5 -2c2.8 -.3 5.5 -1.4 5.5 -6a4.6 4.6 0 0 0 -1.3 -3.2a4.2 4.2 0 0 0 -.1 -3.2s-1.1 -.3 -3.5 1.3a12.3 12.3 0 0 0 -6.2 0c-2.4 -1.6 -3.5 -1.3 -3.5 -1.3a4.2 4.2 0 0 0 -.1 3.2a4.6 4.6 0 0 0 -1.3 3.2c0 4.6 2.7 5.7 5.5 6c-.6 .6 -.6 1.2 -.5 2v3.5"></path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Robot trajectories and logs</h3>
            <p>Paths through cluttered spaces, grasps that fail on ambiguous geometry, or pick sequences that ignore collision. Failure cases from real deployments.</p>
            <div class="example-formats">.csv, .json, .bag</div>
          </div>
          
          <div class="example-card">
            <div class="example-icon">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M15 8h.01"></path>
                <path d="M3 6a3 3 0 0 1 3 -3h12a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v12a3 3 0 0 1 -3 3h-12a3 3 0 0 1 -3 -3v-12z"></path>
                <path d="M3 16l5 -5c.928 -.893 2.072 -.893 3 0l5 5"></path>
                <path d="M14 14l1 -1c.928 -.893 2.072 -.893 3 0l3 3"></path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Geometry imagery</h3>
            <p>Photos of structures with hidden joints, transparent or mirrored materials, ambiguous depth cues, or lighting that breaks segmentation. Occlusion and multi-body contact.</p>
            <div class="example-formats">.jpg, .png, .tiff</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="contribution-note">
          <p><strong>Nothing is live yet.</strong> The upload pipeline is on the <a href="/roadmap">roadmap</a>. Joining the waitlist means you'd be among the first to contribute data when the system opens, helping shape what the benchmark measures and how contributors are credited.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    
    <section id="how">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label">HOW IT WORKS</div>
        <h2>From real-world data to a public score</h2>
        
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-header">
              <div class="step-number">01</div>
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M4 17v2a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2 -2v-2"></path>
                <path d="M7 9l5 -5l5 5"></path>
                <path d="M12 4l0 12"></path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Contribute real-world edge cases</h3>
            <p>Contributors will submit spatial data that models find hard: LiDAR scans, CAD files, robot trajectories and images of real geometry. Rare and complex cases are worth more. Accepted submissions will earn points that record each contributor's share of the archive.</p>
            <ul class="detail-list">
              <li>Planned formats: point clouds (.las, .laz, .ply), CAD (.step, .stl, .obj), trajectories (.csv, .json), images (.jpg, .png).</li>
              <li>Files will be sanitized on intake: metadata stripped, faces and personal information removed.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          
          <div class="step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
          
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-header">
              <div class="step-number">02</div>
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M9 5h-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v12a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2 -2v-12a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-2"></path>
                <path d="M9 3m0 2a2 2 0 0 1 2 -2h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v0a2 2 0 0 1 -2 2h-2a2 2 0 0 1 -2 -2z"></path>
                <path d="M9 14l.01 0"></path>
                <path d="M13 14l.01 0"></path>
                <path d="M9 17l.01 0"></path>
                <path d="M13 17l.01 0"></path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Verify every case before it counts</h3>
            <p>Each submission will go through automated checks for format, duplication and quality, then review by independent human verifiers. A case will enter the benchmark only when reviewers agree on its labels. Reviewers will earn points for accurate reviews.</p>
            <ul class="detail-list">
              <li>Automated checks: file integrity, duplicate detection, label consistency.</li>
              <li>Human review: multiple independent reviewers per case, agreement required.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          
          <div class="step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
          
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-header">
              <div class="step-number">03</div>
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M3 12m0 1a1 1 0 0 1 1 -1h4a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v6a1 1 0 0 1 -1 1h-4a1 1 0 0 1 -1 -1z"></path>
                <path d="M9 8m0 1a1 1 0 0 1 1 -1h4a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v10a1 1 0 0 1 -1 1h-4a1 1 0 0 1 -1 -1z"></path>
                <path d="M15 4m0 1a1 1 0 0 1 1 -1h4a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1 -1 1h-4a1 1 0 0 1 -1 -1z"></path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Score models in public</h3>
            <p>Verified cases will form held-out evaluation sets. Models will be scored on geometric accuracy, structural understanding and physical reasoning, and results will be published on the Spatial Leaderboard with the method used to produce them.</p>
            <ul class="detail-list">
              <li>Metrics include IoU, structural integrity, assembly tree accuracy and physical logic (defined in the leaderboard).</li>
              <li>Model developers will be able to submit through a sandbox API (planned).</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <p class="disclaimer">Points are a record of contribution during the beta. They have no monetary value, and any future use will be decided through the governance process.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    
    <section id="waitlist">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label">EARLY CONTRIBUTOR WAITLIST</div>
        <h2>Be among the first to contribute</h2>
        <p class="intro-text">The upload pipeline isn't built yet. Join the waitlist and we'll email you when it opens. You'll be among the first to upload spatial data and help shape the benchmark.</p>
        
        <WaitlistForm />
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  #hero {
    padding: 160px 0 140px;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at top, rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.05) 0%, transparent 60%);
  }
  
  .hero-content {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr;
    gap: 100px;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 100px;
  }
  
  .hero-text {
    max-width: 620px;
  }
  
  .subhead {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  
  .cta-group {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  
  .hero-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  
  .text-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: var(--transition);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  
  .text-link:hover {
    color: var(--accent-primary);
  }
  
  .text-link svg {
    opacity: 0.6;
    transition: var(--transition);
  }
  
  .text-link:hover svg {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translate(2px, -2px);
  }
  
  .separator {
    color: var(--border-strong);
  }
  
  .hero-visual {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    height: 100%;
  }
  
  .fact-strip {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    padding-top: 100px;
  }
  
  .fact-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 32px 28px;
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    transition: var(--transition);
  }
  
  .fact-item:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-accent);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  
  .fact-item svg {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    opacity: 0.9;
  }
  
  .fact-item span {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  
  .manifesto-body {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 40px 0 56px;
  }
  
  .manifesto-body p {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  
  .manifesto-body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  
  .principles-list {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 48px 0;
    padding-left: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  
  .principles-list li {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    padding: 24px 28px;
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    list-style: none;
    transition: var(--transition);
  }
  
  .principles-list li:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-accent);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }
  
  .principles-list li strong {
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }
  
  .footnote {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    margin-top: 40px;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--border-accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  
  .intro-text {
    max-width: 820px;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  
  #what-to-contribute .intro-text {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;
    gap: 40px;
    margin: 56px 0 48px;
  }
  
  .step {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 32px 28px;
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    transition: var(--transition);
    position: relative;
  }
  
  .step:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-accent);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    transform: translateY(-4px);
  }
  
  .step-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  
  .step-number {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    opacity: 0.15;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  
  .step-header svg {
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    opacity: 0.9;
  }
  
  .step h3 {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }
  
  .step p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  
  .detail-list {
    padding-left: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  
  .detail-list li {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    padding-left: 20px;
    position: relative;
    list-style: none;
  }
  
  .detail-list li::before {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    opacity: 0.6;
  }
  
  .step-arrow {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--border-accent);
    margin-top: 80px;
  }
  
  .disclaimer {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    max-width: 820px;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--border-accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 40px;
    }
    
    .step-arrow {
      display: none;
    }
  }
  
  .contribution-examples {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 28px;
    margin: 48px 0;
  }
  
  .example-card {
    padding: 32px 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    transition: var(--transition);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  
  .example-card::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 3px;
